  "id": "COMPOUND:41012 - PROTEIN:4951",
  "verbalization": "Curcumene is implicated in the biological activity against HL-60 cells through a series of molecular interactions involving Lysine-specific demethylase 2A. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including (2R)-2-[4-(7-Chloroquinoxalin-2-Yl)Oxyphenoxy]Propanoic Acid, Megastigma-4,6(Z),8(Z)-triene, and Notoamide I, all of which have been shown to target HL-60 cells. The shared involvement of Lysine-specific demethylase 2A in these pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which Curcumene exerts its effects on HL-60 cells, possibly through the modulation of epigenetic processes. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Curcumene may act as a modulator of this enzyme, which in turn influences the behavior of HL-60 cells. The consistent targeting of Lysine-specific demethylase 2A by multiple compounds and its role in HL-60 cell activity support the hypothesis that Curcumene could be a potential modulator of this enzyme, thereby contributing to its effects on HL-60 cells.",
